note from Kida:
  the recovered fragment is AES-256-CBC encrypted.

  the password is not stored in this note. it was split into three
  pieces and placed elsewhere in the evidence:
    - piece 1: appears in the pressure-gate log, appended to a hostname
    - piece 2: appears in the sonar-events log, as a scheduled task name
    - piece 3: appears in the vault manifest as the incident reference

  join the three pieces with hyphens to form the password:
      <piece1>-<piece2>-<piece3>

  use openssl to decrypt:
      openssl enc -d -aes-256-cbc -pbkdf2 -iter 100000 -in crystal-fragment.enc -k <password>

  -- Kida, Head of Deep Security
